        "caption": "Catholic Church of Our Lady and St Cuthbert, Prudhoe, Northumberland. This was originally built as a chapel in the grounds of Prudhoe Hall and opened in 1891. Between 1904 and 1905, the church was taken down and transported into the village of Prudhoe where it was rebuilt on its present site in Highfield lane and reopened on 5th October 1905.",
